{
  "id": "peripheral-dyslexia",
  "term": "peripheral dyslexia",
  "definition": "Peripheral dyslexia is a reading disorder in which the difficulty lies mainly in early visual-perceptual, attentional, working-memory, or task-related motor-planning processes involved in recognizing written words, rather than in language-based word meaning or sound conversion. It is a form of acquired dyslexia seen after brain damage and can include patterns such as neglect dyslexia or crowding dyslexia.",
